 "text": "Hi, how are you feeling? Think of it as shorthand for people, and use it with people you know well. It's not for strangers. Also, learn the pronouns people use. Some people only use they, others only use the personal name first, and some switch back and forth. It takes a bit of getting used to, and it' different from English, where we use you all the time. Use the pronoun when you've already established the gender, and use the full form when you unsure. Empty is the correct one. Use which when the answer can be yes or no, and that when you' asking for a yes or no answer.",
